{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek Harness Skin Plugin","id":"gh:1333632856","install_available":false,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-ui-skins","slug":"edwardyang0011/dsh-ui-skins","topics":["deepseek-harness","deepseek-harness-plugin","deepseek-harness-plugins","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugin-verify","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek Harness Skin Plugin"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# @deepseek-ai/dsh-client-ui-skins"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"English | 中文"},{"id":"p4s1","text":"换肤插件（Skin plugin）: registers preset color skins as alias-token themes on the ui-theme service, owns "},{"id":"p4s2","text":"the durable `ui-skins.skin` preference, and registers a Skin row into the settings General section ("},{"id":"p4s3","text":"next to the Appearance row)."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Each preset skin is a `ThemeDefinition` (`{ id, colorScheme, tokens }`) registered through `ctx.them"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"e.register` — the theme registry's sanctioned third-party extension point. The theme presenter appli"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"es the composed tokens as inline CSS variables on `body`, so the skins reuse the entire `--dsw-*` ma"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"chinery (palette switching, `theme/change` snapshots, meta theme-color) without touching any stylesh"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"ery (palette switching, `theme/change` snapshots, meta theme-color) without touching any stylesheet."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"The built-in Appearance row stays the preference authority. The plugin mirrors `theme/change` and ke"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"eps the durable skin id in agreement with whatever preference is live:"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"- picking a preset skin switches the preference to that skin id and persists it under `ui-skins.skin"},{"id":"p7s2","text":"`;
- the **Default** choice restores the built-in preference captured when the skin was picked (or `"},{"id":"p7s3","text":"system` when none was);
- touching the Appearance row (a built-in preference wins) clears the persis"},{"id":"p7s4","text":"ted skin, so the two rows cannot drift — the last write wins."},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Durable schema (`ui-skins`): `skin` ∈ `default | custom | ocean | sakura | forest | midnight` (defau"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"lt `default`), plus the optional `custom` colors section (`scheme`, `accent`, `bgBase`)."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Presets:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"| id | scheme | palette |"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"| `ocean` | light | 蓝绿海洋：海面蓝白底、深青色主色 |
| `sakura` | light | 樱花粉：樱粉白底、玫红主色 |
| `forest` | dark | 松林绿："},{"id":"p11s2","text":"墨绿黑底、翠绿主色 |
| `midnight` | dark | 深空紫：紫黑底、淡紫主色 |"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"Swatch chrome colors live in `SkinRow.module.css`; the token maps in `src/skins.ts` are the theme va"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"h chrome colors live in `SkinRow.module.css`; the token maps in `src/skins.ts` are the theme values."},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Custom colors: the **自定义 (Custom)** swatch opens an editor (base palette, accent, background) that d"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"erives the full token set from two colors via `buildCustomTokenPairs` and stacks it as an `overrideT"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"okens` layer over a registered `custom` theme — editing colors only replaces the layer, switching th"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"e palette re-registers the theme. Colors persist under `ui-skins.custom` and re-apply on boot; an Ap"},{"id":"p13s5","text":"pearance-row write clears the custom skin like any other."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Install this package from the repository (the prebuilt `lib/` is committed):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"Then register the row in your DSH profile patch — `cordis.patch.yml` under `$DSH_HOME/profiles/...`:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"Restart `dsh web` and pick a skin under Settings → General. The peer dependencies match the publishe"},{"id":"p19s2","text":"d `0.1.0-rc.5` dsh family."},{"id":"p20s1","text":"**Host prerequisite:** persistence needs the `ui-skins` namespace on the Host API-proxy's Web settin"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"gs allowlist (`WEB_SETTINGS_NAMESPACES` in dsh-host-apiproxy). Official builds that ship the skin pl"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"ugin include it; a stock build without it rejects the browser's settings writes with `settings-not-e"},{"id":"p20s4","text":"xposed` and every choice resets on refresh."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"## Model Experience"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"None, as skins are a browser-side preference."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"#### KV Cache effect"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"None; this package neither assembles nor sends a provider request."},{"id":"p25s1","text":"## Known Limitations and Deferred Work"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"- **Skins are theme overrides, not full themes** — each skin overrides a curated alias-token set; va"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"lues absent from the override keep the base palette, so a skin does not re-author every surface.
- *"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"*One scheme per skin** — the theme registry pins a `colorScheme` per registered theme, so a skin is "},{"id":"p26s4","text":"either light or dark rather than scheme-aware."}],"truncated":false}
